<title>UK: Abbey National ups 3-year bond to $750 mln.</title>
<headline>Abbey National ups 3-year bond to $750 mln.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond, announced by joint lead managers Credit Suisse First Boston, SBC Warburg and UBS, has been increased to $750 million from $500 million.</p>
<p> BORROWER   ABBEY NATIONAL TREASURY SERVICES PLC</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  ABBEY NATIONAL PLC</p>
<p> AMT ** $750 MLN	COUPON     6.25	MATURITY    31.JAN.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.897   PAY DATE    31.JAN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.375     REOFFER    99.722    SPREAD	+13 BP</p>
<p> NOTES   ** ORIGINALLY LAUNCHED FOR $500 MLN AT 100.965</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    =	   CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  UK	  TAX PROVS   STD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.20	SELL CONC  1.175     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
